cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Cordon: a language-agnostic supply-chain security scanner"
message: "If you use Cordon in research, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Oluwatosin
    family-names: Amokeodo
repository-code: "https://github.com/Threx-code/cordon"
url: "https://github.com/Threx-code/cordon"
abstract: >-
  Cordon scans source trees for supply-chain compromise: malicious and
  vulnerable dependencies across eleven ecosystems, committed credentials,
  obfuscated and second-stage payloads, CI/CD pipeline attacks, and
  infrastructure-as-code misconfiguration. Every detection rule carries the
  samples that prove it fires and the samples that prove it stays quiet, and
  the accuracy claims in its documentation are measured against public corpora
  of real malicious packages rather than asserted.
keywords:
  - supply-chain security
  - static analysis
  - software composition analysis
  - malware detection
  - infrastructure as code
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.4.0
date-released: "2026-09-22"
